   "item": {
    "subject_key": "biology",
    "unit_number": 1,
    "topic_code": "1.2",
    "topic_title": "Elements of Life",
    "stem": "A bacterial culture is moved to a growth medium that contains every nutrient it needs except phosphorus. Which pair of molecules would the cells be unable to newly synthesize, because phosphorus is part of each molecule's structure?",
    "choices": [
     {
      "choice_key": "A",
      "choice_text": "Proteins and DNA",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "This trap assumes that every nitrogen-rich molecule also needs phosphorus. DNA does contain phosphorus, but amino acids are built from C, H, O, N and sometimes S, not phosphorus, so proteins are not the right partner. Fix: For each molecule in a pair, name the element that distinguishes it, such as N or S for proteins and P for nucleic acids."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "B",
      "choice_text": "Glycogen and fats",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "This trap links phosphorus to energy storage, perhaps by thinking of ATP. Glycogen is a polysaccharide and fats are triglycerides, and both are built only from carbon, hydrogen, and oxygen, so neither requires phosphorus. Fix: Ask whether the molecule's building blocks actually include a phosphate group before linking it to phosphorus."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "C",
      "choice_text": "DNA and phospholipids",
      "is_correct": true,
      "rationale": "Each DNA nucleotide includes a phosphate group, and phospholipids carry a phosphate in their hydrophilic head. Without phosphorus, the cells cannot copy their genetic information or build new lipid bilayer, so growth and division stall."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "D",
      "choice_text": "Phospholipids and cholesterol",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "This trap treats every membrane lipid as phosphorus-containing because they sit in the same bilayer. Phospholipids do contain phosphate, but cholesterol is a steroid made of carbon, hydrogen, and oxygen, with no phosphorus. Fix: Check each molecule's own composition instead of assuming that molecules found in the same structure share the same elements."
     }
    ]
   },
